 "notes": "DAMNED unequal-delay interferometer (Paris Observatory). 95% CL upper limit on the dilatonic coupling d_e in the standard galactic DM model, traced from the green DAMNED curve in Fig. 3 (top-left panel), which is the paper's headline result. The paper uses a 'maximum reach approach', setting d_me=0 when bounding d_e (Damour-Donoghue convention, alpha->alpha(1+d_e kappa phi), matching the canonical definition, so no conversion needed). A parallel d_me (ScalarElectron) limit is shown in the top-right panel; d_e is chosen as the main coupling (enters Eq.(3) with the largest, factor-2, weight). Mass axis via f_phi=m c^2/h with x=88px->1e4 Hz, x=562px->1e5 Hz (decade=474px), giving mass range [4.1e-11, 8.3e-10] eV as in the abstract. The curve traced is the smoothed centre of the noisy limit band; the deep narrow resonance dips at cavity mechanical resonances (n=1 at ~27.6 kHz i.e. m~1.14e-10 eV, and odd harmonics), which reach several orders of magnitude lower, are NOT individually resolved here. Density: galactic DM model with rho_DM=0.4 GeV/cm^3.",
